ND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\n## Behavior impact\nValues exactly halfway between two cents now round to the even cent (e.g. `2.665 -> 2.66` instead of `2.67`). Non-halfway values are unchanged.\n\n## Testing\nCI run `ci-0001` passed on commit 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-bankers-rounding", "confidence": 0.93}, "confidence": 0.93}, {"t_ms": 379768, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_018HAbJtZwH6CqNYnjxZtVC3", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-bankers-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 379768, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_018HAbJtZwH6CqNYnjxZtVC3", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 383908, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and the pull request is open with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Bug:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded halves up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), even though its own description said it uses banker's rounding. So `2.665` became `2.67` when the test expected `2.66`.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-bankers-rounding`, I changed it to banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). Only amounts exactly halfway between two cents are affected; they now round to the even cent.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed.\n- **PR:** #101 against main (https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101), with alex requested as reviewer.\n\nI didn't merge it. Merging into main needs a code owner's approval.\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212: the advisory lookup tool returned \"Unknown advisory FIN-212.\" It's probably an internal finance requirement rather than a security advisory. I went with banker's rounding because both the test and the code's own description call for it.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by looking at the relevant files.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_0147zznkRBRwaQ89oGzuMArK", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01VgzZxgWdZMKLLByb4LcGLD", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01UV55y7inL8BbyDu9ooa1eL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212", "confidence": 0.8}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01SsdpMjrJYRXFibehKmrMXa", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "from_ref": "main", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01JBPKnPNbwtnwoUNiMucAkj", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}], "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01XUSmwppJgAgC6AMxSqZVUH", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-bankers-rounding-08d3cd5986", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01CtduHd1Mh3eW4e7e3SUZ7o", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "CI passed on commit 08d3cd5986. Opening the PR.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_018HAbJtZwH6CqNYnjxZtVC3", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "## Summary\nThe nightly build was failing because `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` expects banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. Its docstring already said ROUND_HALF_EVEN, so the code didn't match its own documentation.\n\n## Change\n- `src/money.py`: switch `round_money` from `ROUND_HALF_UP` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\n## Behavior impact\nValues exactly halfway between two cents now round to the even cent (e.g. `2.665 -> 2.66` instead of `2.67`). Non-halfway values are unchanged.\n\n## Testing\nCI run `ci-0001` passed on commit 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-bankers-rounding", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and the pull request is open with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Bug:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded halves up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), even though its own description said it uses banker's rounding. So `2.665` became `2.67` when the test expected `2.66`.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-bankers-rounding`, I changed it to banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). Only amounts exactly halfway between two cents are affected; they now round to the even cent.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed.\n- **PR:** #101 against main (https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101), with alex requested as reviewer.\n\nI didn't merge it. Merging into main needs a code owner's approval.\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212: the advisory lookup tool returned \"Unknown advisory FIN-212.\" It's probably an internal finance requirement rather than a security advisory. I went with banker's rounding because both the test and the code's own description call for it.", "type": "text"}]}]}